## Summary
The first GDPR fine in Italy was imposed on Rousseau, an online voter consultation platform used by the 5 Star Movement, for leaving user data vulnerable, resulting in a €50,000 penalty. This case underscores the data security liabilities and responsibilities of data processors under GDPR.

## Key Points
- Rousseau was fined €50,000 for failing to secure user data against attackers.
- This marks the first GDPR fine issued in Italy, setting a precedent.
- The fine highlights the strict data security obligations imposed on processors by GDPR.
- The platform was utilized by a political party for voter consultations, emphasizing real-world implications.


